  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)=\\int_0^{x^2} \\frac{\\mathrm{t}^2-8 \\mathrm{t}+15}{\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{t}}} \\mathrm{dt}, x \\in \\mathbf{R}$. Then the numbers of local maximum and local minimum points of $f$, respectively, are :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "aoWLw",
      "text": "2 and 3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xclj2",
      "text": "2 and 2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "piIgA",
      "text": "3 and 2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ahLBL",
      "text": "1 and 3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& f(x)=\\int_0^{x^2} \\frac{t^2-8 t+15}{e^t} d t, x \\in R \\\\\n& f^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{x^4-8 x^2+15}{e^{x^2}}(2 x)=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{2 \\times\\left(x^2-5\\right)\\left(x^2-3\\right)}{e^{x^2}}=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow x(x+\\sqrt{5})(x-\\sqrt{5})(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3})=0\n\\end{aligned}$\nBy using wavy curve method\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/_r1Y1-55B6kBNWX7xC6js9Ku_ZaysaTZ0BbartEfY5I.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nNumber of local maximum $=2$\nNumber of local minimum $=3$",
    "image": null
  },
